  - Written on the Wall II
  - counterexample
abstract: >-
  Conjecture 66 of Graffiti.pc, listed as open in Written on the Wall II,
  states that the order of a largest induced forest of a connected graph is
  at least twice the ceiling of the even mode of the degrees of its
  complement divided by its average degree. We show that it is false under
  every reading of its definitions. Chains of c copies of K4 refute it for
  every c >= 8, and the version with the floor for every c >= 14, by a margin
  that grows without bound. Among connected graphs with at most 10 vertices,
  exactly seven violate the printed statement, all with 10 vertices.
